{"kind":"artifact","text":"Implementation report for #15917 at exact clean pushed head 6ca8a06ce5bf98a8de204b3d4d71cf743aa99879 on request/ui-security-headers (one commit over main 5ff8d69c; merges cleanly onto 3b343b78). Recut of 2a273cf8 answering codex's ratified changes-requested verdict 1568df7a. Unchanged: internal/service/browser.go states the policy once (Content-Security-Policy default-src 'none'; script, style, img, font and connect at 'self'; base-uri, form-action, frame-ancestors and object-src 'none'; X-Frame-Options DENY; X-Content-Type-Options nosniff; Referrer-Policy no-referrer); BrowserHeaders applies it in Server.Handler and gs serve applies it outermost, so UI pages, assets, JSON views, not-found answers and the composed refusals all carry it. What changed since 2a273cf8: (a) the verdict's Security finding, that style-src 'self' blocks React's style props, was tested in a real browser and is not so: assert 5bc20ab0 records Google Chrome driven over the DevTools protocol against a served build of this code, page rendered, zero policy violations, a CSSOM write applied, and a control setAttribute('style') refused with a hash matching the probe. CSP style-src governs style attributes and elements in markup and setAttribute, not the CSSOM through which React applies the style prop. Per the verdict's alternative repair, the middleware comment and docs/reference/gs/serve.md now state that style contract explicitly. (b) Per the verdict's Simplification, the bundle regex check in TestEmbeddedUILoadsUnderTheBrowserPolicy is deleted: its premise (that CSSOM edits are blocked) was wrong, so it asserted a rule the browser does not enforce. The test still loads index.html and every script, stylesheet, icon and font it names through the served embed, refuses inline script, style and handlers in the markup, refuses non-same-origin, data: or remote references in the stylesheet, and refuses any asset whose declared content type nosniff would reject. TestEveryResponseClassCarriesTheBrowserPolicy is unchanged: all four headers, policy pinned as a literal, on a UI page, the icon, a JSON view, a JSON refusal, a not-found answer and the trusted-host refusal through the resident's composition; removing the middleware fails it. No browser is added to the Go gate; the browser assertion is a recorded check, not a test. Gates at this head: go vet ./internal/service/ clean, go test -count=1 ./internal/service/ ok (29.5s); the earlier full-suite run at 2a273cf8 covered every other package and this recut touches only internal/service and docs beyond it. Embed unchanged. Rests-On #15917. Co-signed artifacts follow at cmd/gs and the three docs.","body":{"branch":"request/ui-security-headers","commit":"6ca8a06ce5bf98a8de204b3d4d71cf743aa99879","path":"internal/service"}}